<title>USA: First Data Q4 oper shr $0.44 vs $0.32.</title>
<headline>First Data Q4 oper shr $0.44 vs $0.32.</headline>
<dateline>HACKENSACK, N.J. 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>FIRST DATA CORPORATION</p>
<p>			  (In millions, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>					Three Months Ended December 31,</p>
<p>						 1996	1995  % Change</p>
<p> Operating Revenues		     $1,349.6  $1,119.1    21%</p>
<p> Total Revenues			    1,349.6   1,119.1    21%</p>
<p>Income Before Income Taxes</p>
<p> Before nonrecurring charge		332.3     240.9    38%</p>
<p> Merger, integration and impairment     29.8   (645.7)</p>
<p>						   362.1   (404.8)</p>
<p>Net Income</p>
<p> Before nonrecurring charge		206.0     150.2    37%</p>
<p>Merger, integration and impairment,</p>
<p>net of tax</p>
<p>($11.5 expense-1996, $105.8</p>
<p>     benefit-1995)			    18.3   (539.9)</p>
<p>						   224.3  ( 389.7)</p>
<p>Earnings (Loss) Per Common Share</p>
<p> Before nonrecurring charge		 0.44	0.32    38%</p>
<p> Merger, integration and impairment     0.04    (1.20)</p>
<p>						    0.48   ( 0.88)</p>
<p> Weighted Average Shares		   475.8     445.2</p>
<p>				     Twelve Months Ended December 31,</p>
<p>						 1996	1995  % Change</p>
<p> Operating Revenues		     $4,934.1  $4,081.2    21%</p>
<p> Total Revenues			    4,938.1   4,186.2    18%</p>
<p>Income Before Income Taxes</p>
<p> Before nonrecurring charge	    1,018.3     813.3    25%</p>
<p> Merger, integration and impairment     13.5   (645.7)</p>
<p>						 1,031.8     167.6</p>
<p>Net Income</p>
<p> Before nonrecurring charge		628.2     455.7    38%</p>
<p>Merger, integration and impairment, net of tax</p>
<p>($5.2 expense-1996, $105.8</p>
<p>    benefit-1996)				8.3   (539.9)</p>
<p>						   636.5   ( 84.2)</p>
<p>Earnings (Loss) Per Common Share</p>
<p> Before nonrecurring charge		 1.35	1.02    32%</p>
<p> Merger, integration and impairment     0.02    (1.21)</p>
<p>						    1.37   ( 0.19)</p>
<p> Weighted Average Shares		   475.7     434.0    10%</p>
<p>NOTE: Pretax income for the year was $1.03 billion compared with $168 million in 1995, which included a $646 million charge in the fourth quarter of 1995 related to nonrecurring merger, integration and impairment costs.  </p>
<p>Results in 1996 include a $46 million gain on the divestiture of MoneyGram in the fourth quarter and $32 million of merger, integration and impairment charges ($16 million in the fourth quarter).</p>
<p>The Company reported net income of $637 million for the year versus an after tax loss of $84 million in 1995. Excluding the gain and charges in both years, First Data's net income for the year was $628 million, up 38% from 1995's $456 million.</p>
